# 🛡️ Recall Radar — Product-Safety AI Agent

**Databricks AI Bootcamp Capstone** — an agentic product-safety assistant that
monitors live FDA recall data, semantically matches recalls to products people
own, scores severity, and takes real actions (writes alerts). Anyone can search
recalls by meaning or keep a watchlist of products to monitor — no login
required.

> ⚠️ Informational awareness only, not official safety or medical advice.
> Always verify with the manufacturer or the FDA and follow official guidance.

## What it does

- **Search recalls by meaning:** "undeclared peanuts", "salmonella in flour",
  "listeria" → the most semantically relevant FDA recalls, ranked, with severity.
- **Watchlist monitoring:** add products (food/drug/device/vehicle) to a
  labeled watchlist; the agent matches them against recalls and **writes alerts**
  with a severity and a recommended action.
- **Two ways to use it:** a web app (recall search + a save-by-name watchlist
  that checks your foods against current recalls) and an AI agent (natural-
  language chat via Databricks Agent Bricks).
- **Honest matching:** results are gated by a similarity threshold, so an
  unrelated query (e.g. a product with no matching recall) returns "no recalls
  found" instead of a misleading weak match.

## Architecture

```
┌ INGEST (Spark) ─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  openFDA food enforcement API (keyless)                      │
│  → Spark DataFrame: parse JSON, normalize, build recall_id   │
│  → Lakebase `recalls`                                         │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        │
┌ EMBED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Databricks-hosted gte-large-en endpoint (1024-dim)          │
│  → Lakebase `recall_embeddings` (VECTOR(1024) + HNSW)        │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        │
┌ SERVE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  MCP server (FastMCP, Databricks App)  ── Agent Bricks agent │
│    search_recalls · add_product · check_watchlist · list_alerts│
│  Flask dashboard (Databricks App)      ── web search UI       │
│  both read/write Lakebase; queries embedded via gte-large-en  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Capstone requirements — how each is met

| Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Spark data pipeline** | `ingest_recalls` notebook: Spark reads openFDA JSON, normalizes to the `recalls` schema, writes to Lakebase. |
| **Third-party API** | openFDA food enforcement (recalls) + Databricks Foundation Model API (gte-large-en embeddings). Both keyless from within Databricks. |
| **Unstructured data processing** | Free-text recall reason + product + firm embedded to 1024-dim vectors for semantic retrieval (pgvector cosine). |
| **Databricks App with frontend** | `recall-radar-dashboard` — Flask web UI: a recall search page (ranked cards with color-coded severity badges) plus a save-by-name watchlist page (add foods → saved-products table → recall matches). |
| **AI agent (read + write)** | Agent Bricks agent over the MCP server: **reads** (search_recalls, list_alerts) and **writes** (add_product, check_watchlist → creates alerts). |

## The agent's tools

| Tool | R/W | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `search_recalls(query, top_k)` | READ | Semantic search over recalls (pgvector). |
| `add_product(label, kind, name, brand)` | WRITE | Add a product to a watchlist (no login; label is user-chosen). |
| `check_watchlist(label)` | READ+WRITE | Match watchlist products to recalls; create alerts with severity + recommended action. |
| `list_alerts(label)` | READ | List alerts for a watchlist. |

**Severity** comes from the FDA recall classification: Class I → High,
Class II → Medium, Class III → Low. Each alert includes a recommended action
(e.g. "Class I recall — stop using immediately and contact the firm").

## Lakebase schema

`recalls`, `recall_embeddings` (VECTOR(1024) + HNSW), `watchlists`,
`watched_products`, `alerts`. See `schema.sql`.

## Data source + why

**openFDA** (food enforcement) — free, keyless, weekly-updated FDA recall data
with a built-in severity signal (Class I/II/III). No secrets anywhere in the
project. Query embedding uses the **Databricks-hosted gte-large-en** endpoint so
no embedding model runs inside the app (avoids the app-memory limit).

**Confidence threshold.** Both the search page and the watchlist matcher require
a cosine similarity of at least ~0.68 before surfacing a recall. This separates
true product matches (which score ~0.70+) from generic food-adjacency (~0.62-
0.66), so an unrelated query returns "no recalls found" rather than a
misleading weak match — the honest behaviour a safety tool should have.

